YM2608 internal rhythm sample reconstruction
===========================================

Source: ValleyBell/libvgm, emu/cores/fmopn_2608rom.h
Revision: c8b998b606895990c409a512b86c5509070f9f0d
https://github.com/ValleyBell/libvgm/blob/c8b998b606895990c409a512b86c5509070f9f0d/emu/cores/fmopn_2608rom.h

The header is copied unchanged. Its upstream comment describes reconstruction
from the chip's output, verified against a real YM2608. It is not a game asset.
The 8192 data bytes have CRC32 23c9e0d8 and SHA1
50b6c3e288eaa12ad275d4f323267bb72b0445df.

License: GPL-2.0-or-later, following the fmopn.c core that includes this table:
https://github.com/ValleyBell/libvgm/blob/c8b998b606895990c409a512b86c5509070f9f0d/emu/cores/fmopn.c
That source states "license:GPL-2.0+" and names the copyright holders:
Jarek Burczynski and Tatsuyuki Satoh (MultiArcadeMachineEmulator development).
See LICENSE for the GNU General Public License version 2.

This data is kept separate from the BSD-3-Clause YMFM core. Makoto supplies it
to YMFM through the existing ADPCM-A memory callback. The optional external
rhythm ROM remains an override, including when restoring older saved machines.
No YMFM engine code or serialized state layout changes are needed for the table.
